# Config and CLI

- A real Appwrite app (schema, functions, sites, CI) lives in `appwrite.config.json`. Init once; then pull/push. Do not pass `appwrite client --project-id` on every project command when the config already names the project.
- Keep `appwrite.config.json` in sync automatically whenever work needs new or changed Appwrite resources: functions, tables, columns, buckets, permissions, teams, topics, sites, and related settings. Update the config in the **same** change as the code/types that use those resources so the project is immediately pushable with the CLI (`appwrite push …`) when the user asks to deploy.
- Do not leave schema or resource changes only in code or only in the Console — the config file is the source of truth for what can be pushed.
- For CLI details: skill `appwrite-cli`. For the TypeScript SDK: skill `appwrite-typescript`.
- Stack choices (React, Tailwind, monorepo, etc.) follow the **project**, not this plugin. Do not force a UI kit or CSS framework.
